  - canine cognition
  - DogFACS
  - semantic grounding
  - interspecies interaction
  - survey
abstract: >
  An evidence-bounded survey asking how far we are from translating what
  dogs say. It introduces a five-rung translation ladder (signal, affect,
  intent, reference, dialogue), synthesizes canine behavioral biology,
  cross-species decoding projects (CETI, DolphinGemma, Earth Species
  Project), and the commercial pet-translator landscape, and identifies a
  semantic gap and a falsifiability crisis. Conclusion: validated
  affect-and-intent inference is plausible this decade; faithful open-ended
  translation of canine language may be permanently ill-posed.